.TH ESDM\-ES\-EXT\-SERVE 8 "2026-10-16" "ESDM @VERSION@" "ESDM Manual"
.SH NAME
esdm\-es\-ext\-serve \- serve an external entropy source plugin to the ESDM
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B esdm\-es\-ext\-serve
.B \-\-plugin
.I LIBRARY
.B \-\-socket
.I PATH
.RB [ \-\-mode
.IR MODE ]
.RB [ \-\-client_uid
.IR USER ]...
.RB [ \-\-name
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-entropy_rate
.IR BITS ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B esdm\-es\-ext\-serve
loads the external entropy source plugin library
.I LIBRARY
\- see
.BR libesdm_es_ext (3)
\- and serves it on the UNIX domain socket
.IR PATH ,
which
.B esdm\-server \-\-es_ext_socket
.I PATH
connects to. The plugin that
.B esdm\-server \-\-es_ext_lib
would load into the daemon runs in a process of its own this way: with its
own privileges, in its own address space, and restarted on its own.
.PP
The plugin is loaded and initialized before the socket is served; a plugin
library that cannot be loaded, exports no plugin of the supported version or
fails its initialization ends the program with exit status 1. It serves until
it receives
.BR SIGTERM ,
.B SIGINT
or
.BR SIGHUP ,
then removes the socket and exits with status 0.
.PP
The ESDM accepts a provider running as root, or as the user given with
.BR "esdm\-server \-\-es_ext_socket_uid" .
It connects with its privileges dropped once a connection was lost, so the
socket has to let the user the ESDM runs as connect \- by default
.BR nobody ,
hence the default mode 0666. A more restrictive mode needs the ESDM to run with
a group that is granted access
.RB ( "esdm\-server \-\-groupname" ).
.PP
The name of the plugin \- or the one given with
.B \-\-name
\- is the name the ESDM shows the source under, which it asks the provider for
on every connection (INFO request, see
.BR libesdm_es_ext (3)).
.PP
The rate the plugin declares with its
.I entropy_rate
callback \- or the one given with
.B \-\-entropy_rate
\- is the entropy rate the ESDM credits the provider at, unless a rate is
configured for the source in the ESDM
.RB ( "esdm\-server \-\-es_ext_socket_entropy_rate" ),
which takes precedence. Without either, the provider declares none and the ESDM
credits it at 0 unless configured otherwise. Note that whoever runs a provider
of a user the ESDM accepts can declare any rate this way: the ESDM operator
who does not want to trust that configures the rate of the source. The rate
the plugin declares is logged at start up.
.PP
The status the plugin reports of itself, if it has a
.I status_json
callback, is handed to the ESDM, which shows it in its own status.
.PP
In turn, only clients running as root or as a user given with
.B \-\-client_uid
are served \- by default root and
.BR nobody ,
the user the ESDM runs as unless told otherwise. Any other client is
disconnected at once, so that it can neither take the few client slots the
ESDM needs nor drain the noise source.
.PP
Up to 8 clients are served at a time. When all slots are taken and another
client connects, the client that sent nothing for the longest time is
disconnected to make room for it, so that clients of an allowed user holding
their slots without using them cannot lock the ESDM out: the ESDM connects
again at once when it finds its connection closed, and gets a slot back the
same way. A client running as root makes room only for another client running
as root, as the ESDM connects as root at start up; a client that finds no
slot is disconnected at once.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-plugin " \fILIBRARY\fR"
Plugin library of the entropy source.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-socket " \fIPATH\fR"
Socket to serve it on. A socket left at the path by an earlier instance is
replaced, any other file is not.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mode " \fIMODE\fR"
Access mode of the socket, octal. The default is 0666.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-client_uid " \fIUSER\fR"
Serve clients running as
.I USER
\- a uid or a user name \- next to root. May be given up to 8 times; the
default is
.BR nobody .
Give the user of
.B esdm\-server \-\-username
if the ESDM runs as another one.
.TP
.BI \-\-name " NAME"
Declare
.I NAME
as the name of the source in place of the name of the plugin: 1 to 32 bytes of
UTF-8 without control characters. A name that is none of that is refused at
start up, with exit status 1.
.TP
.BI \-\-entropy_rate " BITS"
Declare
.I BITS
of entropy per 256 bits of data, 0 to 256, as the rate of the source in place
of the one of the plugin. Anything else is refused at start up, with exit
status 1.
.TP
.B \-\-no_dtls
Do not offer DTLS to the clients. A build with DTLS (meson option
.BR dtls )
offers it by default, see
.BR libesdm_es_ext (3).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Verbose logging; repeat for more.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH SEVERAL SOURCES
One
.B esdm\-es\-ext\-serve
serves one plugin. An ESDM built with several provider socket sources (meson
option
.BR es_ext_socket_num )
reads several providers, one per source: run one
.B esdm\-es\-ext\-serve
per plugin, each on a socket of its own, and give the ESDM one
.B \-\-es_ext_socket
per socket, the n-th for its n-th source \- see
.BR esdm\-server (8).
The processes are independent of each other: each is restarted, and fails, on
its own, and the ESDM credits each of them at the rate configured for its
source.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
esdm\-es\-ext\-serve \-\-plugin /usr/lib/esdm/my_es.so \\
	\-\-socket /run/esdm\-es\-ext.socket
esdm\-server \-\-es_ext_socket /run/esdm\-es\-ext.socket
.fi
.PP
Two plugins, served to an ESDM with two provider socket sources:
.PP
.nf
esdm\-es\-ext\-serve \-\-plugin /usr/lib/esdm/a.so \-\-socket /run/esdm\-es\-a.socket
esdm\-es\-ext\-serve \-\-plugin /usr/lib/esdm/b.so \-\-socket /run/esdm\-es\-b.socket
esdm\-server \-\-es_ext_socket /run/esdm\-es\-a.socket \\
	\-\-es_ext_socket /run/esdm\-es\-b.socket
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libesdm_es_ext (3),
.BR esdm\-server (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Markus Theil <theil.markus@gmail.com>
